<urn:raiden:resurrection:mimir:molocule:definition:2026-10-15:r8>
        a                    core:DefinitionRevision;
        dct:created          "2026-10-15"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date>;
        dct:isVersionOf      <urn:raiden:resurrection:mimir:molocule>;
        dct:subject          <https://w3id.org/gil-next/atom/04c656ec-cb62-4e20-aed6-1e5e55237875>;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote>
                "Same wording as r7; the revision now names its subject, the permanent Molocule Atom (r7 named only its series)."@en;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition>
                "A Molocule is a deterministic grammar-derived, source-qualified ordered expression. G0002(Tyr, Oceana) produces †Oceana; G0002(Tyr, Hephaestus) produces †Hephaestus; G0002(Tyr, Athena) produces †Athena, provided their operand identities and applicability are qualified. Molocule identity is based on the grammar family and ordered constituent identities; the display notation and applicable meanings are independently versioned and do not remint the structural Molocule."@en;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote>
                "Tyr Oceana under G0001 and †Oceana under G0002 have different structural signatures; use only the latter for Tyr's unary governance function. Reversion from † to § changes presentation and the qualifier meaning revision but NOT the Tyr Atom identifier or the signature of G0002(Tyr, subject). Actual governance execution is not implied by the expression."@en;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom  <https://api.github.com/repos/tevintay249-stack/Raiden/git/blobs/8b0caaef33ae34edcbf3edd2d11cc7baadc0f2c0> , <https://github.com/tevintay249-stack/Raiden/blob/896675deac88192600e3d27a93545b733226d598/spec/mimir/atom-molocule-meaning-2026-10-15/r8.candidate.trig>;
        prov:wasRevisionOf   <urn:raiden:resurrection:mimir:molocule:definition:2026-10-14:r7> .

